 (ask ≥0.80, ≤50s left) + favorite ask continuously >0.55 for 90s + hard stop below 0.50, 5% equity","new":"A’s late favorite (ask ≥0.80) allowed from ≤70s left + favorite ask continuously >0.55 for 60s + hard stop below 0.50, 5% equity","reason":"The 90s confirm was not the main live blocker (0 filter_blocks; two late favorites held ~89s but could not fill into a one-sided late book). Shortening the confirm to 60s eases that filter. Allowing the same ≥0.80 late-favorite price rule from 70s left (instead of 50s) aims to lift an ask before the late book goes one-sided. A 1-minute backtest of slightly earlier late entries stayed strongly positive; a looser 120s-left proxy was still positive but weaker, so the late gate stops at 70s. Hard stop and sizing are unchanged. A’s own 50s late-favorite rule is unchanged."},{"time_pt":"6:36 PM PT Nov 10","account":"M5","old":"T’s 60–150s / 45–60¢ rule, plus 3 consecutive polls where book imbalance I is strictly on the same side (I>0 for UP, I<0 for DOWN), $5","new":"Same T entry rule, plus 2 consecutive polls where I > −0.25 for UP or I < +0.25 for DOWN, $5","reason":"Zero trades in ~26 hours even though T filled three times in that span. On all three of those T fills, top-of-book imbalance I was on the opposite side (or nearly flat), so a strict same-side I>0 / I<0 filter could never agree. Lowered the agreement floor from 0 to −0.25 / +0.25 and required 2 agreeing snapshots instead of 3. That would have allowed 2 of T’s 3 live trades (the UP fill at I=−0.25 would still be blocked). Expected rate approaches T’s when the book is not strongly opposed (T’s 18-day backtest is ~10 trades/day / +$115 at $5; live T has been quieter)."}],"coinbase_lag":{"reachable":true,"samples":900,"last_price":74465.48,"last_diff_bp":-2.3026,"mean_abs_bp":2.0949},"maker_fill_rule":"Resting bid at P fills only when that side's best ask is strictly below P (traded through). Touch is not a fill; bid dropping below P is not a fill."}
